-- Loan and Rental each take the fields of Borrowing, so `member` and `dueOn` are declared once,
-- on Borrowing. Rule MoveLoan gives a loan to another member by setting the loan's `member`.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes":
--
--   ### Member
--   - Time passing can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateBorrowing.
--   - Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithLateBorrowing.
--
--   ### Loan
--   - A new Member can now make a Loan become a LoanOfLateMember.
--   - A new Member can now make a Loan stop being a LoanOfLateMember.
--
-- Four things are wrong. No line says MoveLoan can make a Member become or stop being a
-- MemberWithLateBorrowing, though moving a late loan does both. No line says MoveLoan can make
-- a Loan become or stop being a LoanOfLateMember, though the loan's member changes. No line
-- says a new Loan or a new Rental can make a Member become a MemberWithLateBorrowing. And a
-- new Member cannot change which member an existing Loan names. The same spec with `member`
-- and `dueOn` declared on Loan itself draws the MoveLoan lines and the new Loan line.
act Member { name: text }

shape Borrowing {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

act Loan is Borrowing { title: text }

act Rental is Borrowing { fee: integer }

transient act Transfer {
    loan: one Loan
    receiver: one Member
}

rule MoveLoan when Transfer {
    loan.member = receiver
}

shape MemberWithLateBorrowing = Member where exists (borrowings where dueOn < today)

shape LoanOfLateMember = Loan where member.name == "late"
